      "model": "gpt-6.2-sol",
      "output": "{\n  \"choice\": \"within\",\n  \"base_and_horizon\": {\n    \"text\": \"Nintendo guided to JPY 200,000 million in consolidated profit attributable to owners of parent for the fiscal year ending March 31, 2021 (PDF pp. 2 and 4). My base case is that full-year actual profit lands within ±2% of that guide, inclusive.\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P1\", \"P4\"]\n  },\n  \"causal_driver\": {\n    \"text\": \"Nintendo reported that production and shipping delays were easing, though continued shortages of necessary components could disrupt supply (PDF p. 3). Management assumed it could meet full-year demand and release software on schedule (p. 4). My base case is that recovering component supply lets Nintendo make up enough delayed Switch shipments by year-end to keep sales and parent-attributable profit near plan.\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P3\", \"P4\", \"P5\"]\n  },\n  \"alternative\": {\n    \"text\": \"Lower: if component shortages persist, Nintendo may be unable to recover lost Switch hardware sales by March 31, 2021. Fewer new Switch owners would also limit sales of the planned software lineup, making a profit miss beyond the tolerance plausible (PDF pp. 3–4).\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P3\", \"P4\", \"P5\"]\n  },\n  \"revision_signal\": {\n    \"text\": \"I would switch to lower if a pre-year-end earnings update materially cuts the full-year Switch hardware unit forecast because of component shortages and says the lost shipments cannot be made up by year-end. That would directly contradict the full-year supply recovery assumed in the guide (PDF pp. 3–4).\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P3\", \"P4\", \"P5\"]\n  },\n  \"historical_comparison\": {\n    \"text\": \"The JPY 200,000 million guide was 22.7% below the just-reported fiscal year ended March 31, 2020, per Nintendo’s published consolidated year-over-year comparison. The JPY 210,842 million figure on the same page is non-consolidated profit, not the comparable prior-year figure (PDF p. 2).\",\n    \"evidence_ids\": [\"P1\", \"P2\"]\n  }\n}",
